":"https://api.github.com/users/jrhone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrhone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrhone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrhone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrhone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrhone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrhone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-09-30T17:20:09Z","updated_at":"2019-09-30T17:22:23Z","body":"Hi j4th,\r\n\r\nI'm having trouble reproducing the issue, could you provide more detailed reproduction steps?\r\nA larger snippet that results in the error being thrown, or your entire app would be ideal.\r\n\r\nWith that said, Plotly v4 changed its main package and is accessed differently than in v3.\r\n\r\nWith v4\r\n\r\n```import chart_studio.plotly as ply```\r\n\r\nWith v3\r\n\r\n```import plotly.plotly as ply```\r\n\r\nPlease verify the version you're using and access the Plotly object accordingly. Streamlit apps should work with both versions.\r\n\r\nCheck version\r\n```\r\nimport plotly\r\nplotly.__version__\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo install v4\r\n```\r\npip install chart-studio\r\npip install plotly==4\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo install v3\r\n```\r\npip install plotly==3\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso, looks like you're on version `0.45.0` of Streamlit, feel free to update to `0.46.0` with `pip install --upgrade streamlit` if there's no blockers on your end.\r\n\r\nLet us know if you're still having issues afterwards.\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamlit/streamlit/issues/comments/536661702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jrhone","id":699897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5OTg5Nw==","ava